WEBVTT

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.780
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:31.120
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:38.890
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:45.000
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.770
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:57.480
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:04.450
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:12.390
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:20.060
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.150
Aah, this is great! I'm sure glad
we decided to go for a drive.

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.850
Right, Natsumi?

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:56.530
Natsumi?

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.530
Wow! What a nice
looking fish!

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.410
It's huge! I didn't know you could catch
such big fish around here. Wow!

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.210
Want to give
it a try?

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:08.510
Really? You don't
mind? I'd love to!

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:10.410
Thanks
a lot!

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:12.640
I thought we were supposed
to be on a drive.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.260
Change of plans! I want to fish!

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.920
I don't believe you...

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.890
Here goes nothing!

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.560
Give 'em lots
of bait.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.800
Won't have to worry about
dinner tonight!

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.940
Sure about
that?

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:37.910
Maybe not, huh.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.580
Miyuki, should we start heading ba...

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.480
Rats!

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.450
Huh?

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:45.350
Huh?
It took off with my bait again!

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:45.420
It took off with my bait again!

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.910
Oh, dear...

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:50.890
I think I've got the feel of this.
So where am I going wrong?

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.720
Whose idea was
this, anyway?!

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.670
Oops. Mine.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.470
All right, this time I'll do it!

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.130
Hey.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.610
Excuse me, but haven't we
met somewhere before?

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.570
My hat!
My hat!

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.700
Look out!

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.510
We've got to save him!

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:43.480
Wait! He's coming up!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.720
What a daredevil.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.690
I'll say.

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:59.320
What?! It's him!

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:04.400
FILE. 38
THAT MAN,
SHOUJI TOUKAIRIN

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:10.060
You've already met
him before...

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:14.370
...he is the officer who was a great help
in the incident at the Tokyo Tower.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.270
There seems to be a few people
missing, but let's begin.

00:04:25.850 --> 00:04:29.480
Ew, I feel terrible!
What a hangover.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:34.700
Tsujimoto! Kobayakawa!
Get over here, pronto!

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.830
Yes, sir!
Yes, sir!

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.470
Uh...

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.470
As I mentioned
last week...

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.100
...he's here from
headquarters...

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.770
...as part of the rescue
training.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.040
The exercises will commence
tomorrow.

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:57.420
I am Lt. Shouji
Toukairin.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.510
He's an instructor?

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.120
Lieutenant?

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:04.090
Lieutenant?
So he's higher in rank than us.

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:11.330
Boy, this won't
be easy.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:12.800
What won't?

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.330
Not one thing in particular, just generally.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:18.200
I don't know what you're saying.
And I don't think you do, either.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:21.810
Maybe you're right. Let's go back
and get something to eat.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.880
Thought you had
a hangover?

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.980
Just the time for a bowl of curried
rice or spicy tofu and rice!

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.280
Or rice and
tempura!

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.380
All right!

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:40.890
A nice big bowl of Chinese
rice and veggies!

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.290
"Chinese Rice - Sold Out"

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:42.830
Oh, well. Fried rice,
large. Huh?

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:44.890
"Ramen - Sold Out"

00:05:44.890 --> 00:05:45.000
Oh, well. Fried rice,
large. Huh?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.400
"Fried Rice (Large) - Sold Out"

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.060
What?!

00:05:49.170 --> 00:05:54.160
Miso, pork and vegetables on rice, udon,
porkchops on rice, assorted deep fry...

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:58.510
Oh my God, everything's sold out.
Isn't there anything left?!

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:01.940
Looks like it's just sand-
wiches and salads.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:05.420
How am I supposed
to get full on that?

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:07.780
I'm sure you'll
be fine.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.480
My stomach's another
matter.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.340
I'll wrestle you!

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.830
I'll wrestle you!
What?!

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:30.200
Hey!

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:34.940
If I lose, you get to have Miyuki's
homemade lunch here.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:36.640
Let's go.

00:06:36.820 --> 00:06:38.320
Natsumi, that's my lunch!

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.010
I can't, Tsujimoto.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:44.250
I've got a busy day ahead, and I don't
know when I'll be able to eat next!

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.990
Come on! Someone...
Anyone...

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:52.230
Anybody want to take me on? Come
on, who wants to wrestle, huh?

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.860
She's nuts. Who'd
want to do that?

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:56.470
Go give it a shot.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:07:00.200
I don't want to give up my lunch.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:04.780
There'd be no
competition.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:14.450
I'm going to have some ramen, a
bowl of rice and grilled eggplant.

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:16.610
Hmm?

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:18.850
Wha?!

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:22.390
In the red corner,
Shouji Toukairin.

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.360
In the blue corner, Natsumi
Tsujimoto!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.170
This'll be fair
and square.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:40.080
Are you both
ready?

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.020
Ready?

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:47.090
Go!

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:58.100
Look at that!

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.830
Look at that!
They're not even moving!

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.270
He's a match
for Natsumi.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.770
Natsumi's losing.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:16.780
Only sandwiches
and salads?!

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:19.650
I've lived 50
years and...

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:23.820
...I haven't made it all this
way for that kind of stuff!

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.450
And the winner is,
Lt. Toukairin!

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:31.460
Wait a second, Nakajima!
It's not over yet!

00:08:31.630 --> 00:08:34.000
Your elbow.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.330
Your elbow's
off the table.

00:08:39.110 --> 00:08:42.410
Precisely! Tsujimoto breaks
a rule, and loses the battle!

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.810
That must have been
a blow to her.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:21.880
Still, she's been sitting like that for ages.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:25.750
Still, she's been sitting like that for ages.
Do you think she's all right?

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:30.490
It's just the precursor to the big
storm. She isn't through yet.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:35.230
Something is going to
happen. Hmm?

00:09:35.560 --> 00:09:37.130
Tsujimoto.

00:09:37.130 --> 00:09:38.690
Tsujimoto.
Hmm?

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.990
Ch... Chief!

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:42.970
I apologize for my per-
formance earlier!

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.130
Uh...

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.930
My failure is in-
excusable!

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.440
I will repent and
work hard...

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:58.250
...to restore your name and win
the battle! Excuse me, sir!

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.750
Uh, Tsujimoto...

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.390
I wonder where
she's going?

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:08.720
Where she always
goes to think.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.460
Something is definitely
going to happen.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:23.740
"Training Room"

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:29.080
...998... 999...

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.650
Are you still at it?

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:33.250
Are you still at it?
Got a while to go! Don't wait up for me.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.920
You're overdoing it.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.980
You're overdoing it.
I have a reputation to uphold.

00:10:38.090 --> 00:10:40.930
His hobbies are fishing
and rock climbing.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:45.990
He enjoys sleeping and eating. He's
4th level kendo. First level abacus.

00:10:47.270 --> 00:10:51.330
He's 23 years old, but we
have the same birthday.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.410
He likes bananas.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:11:00.570
He is 169 cm. tall, weighs 57 kg...
same as an average guy... 1000!

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:02.720
Huh?!

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:11.390
You must have found
out from Yoriko.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.220
You've gotta know
your enemy.

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:15.930
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:19.230
Don't push yourself too hard.
That's it? You're not helping me here?

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:25.230
Help you, huh?

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:31.800
Good luck.

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:43.450
Sure it isn't a
little early?

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:47.560
The key is to work out before
I go on duty! Hey!

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.790
Look at that!

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:54.890
He must be working
out, too!

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.800
See you later!

00:11:56.970 --> 00:11:58.940
Bye.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.550
Shoot.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:13.820
Come on, let's
get movin'!

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:24.900
Come on, pal. Get
out of my way!

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:37.110
Oh, no! Not another red light!
I'll have to take a short cut.

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:39.810
No!

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:55.860
Jeez, I don't
believe this.

00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:58.430
Huh?

00:13:03.640 --> 00:13:05.300
Officer Tsujimoto.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.430
Aww!

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:13.240
Morning.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:15.380
Uh, good
morn...

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:20.550
"Please adopt this little puppy!"

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.460
I sure hope somebody
wants him.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:26.850
It won't take him long to
win someone's heart.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:30.400
I'll leave him with you, then!

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.590
You don't have to be so formal!

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.600
<i>Oops. I shouldn't show</i>
<i>my weakness.</i>

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:43.840
Lieutenant Toukairin. What kind of
training are we having today?

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:48.350
Training? Uh... I don't know,
just the usual...

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.380
No.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:50.420
Pardon?

00:13:50.420 --> 00:13:52.820
I want you to run me through the wringer!

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:56.550
What's the point, if you don't
give us a good run for it?

00:13:56.720 --> 00:13:57.730
Uh...

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.690
Well, see you later.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.010
Good morning!

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:20.540
All right, give me all you've got!

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:25.790
"Mental Attitude in Emergency
Situations"

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:27.580
A report!
"Mental Attitude in Emergency
Situations"

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:31.050
"If it's heavy, put all your
strength into it."

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.900
Do you have a question?

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:40.920
Do you have a question?
No, sir.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.860
Umm, I think this
is a bit much.

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:47.310
Stay still, I told you.

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.180
This is what happens...

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.080
Huh?

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:52.110
This happens when you try to rush it.

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.340
Yes.

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:55.850
Excuse me?

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.020
Yes?

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.180
Enough with this classroom stuff!

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:02.380
Police need hands-on
training!

00:15:03.190 --> 00:15:06.160
If you're going to train us, how about
a more realistic, more concrete...

00:15:06.330 --> 00:15:08.700
...something more practical... uh...

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.930
So out of character, she forgot her lines.

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.260
Well, what I'm trying to say is,
how about something harder.

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.840
You mean simulation training.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:16.800
Yes! That's it!

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.570
You sure are determined,
aren't you?

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:32.120
You bet! We need to be capable in extreme
situations. We need extreme training.

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:36.020
And the real
motivation?

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:40.460
Until now it's just been meaning-
less competition...

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:46.690
...but when it comes to simulation
training, you'll see!

00:15:47.330 --> 00:15:49.630
It's time to go, Miyuki!

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.130
Okay.

00:15:59.380 --> 00:16:03.910
Today we're going to practice removing
victims from car accidents.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:05.850
Yes, sir!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:10.720
Okay, say that the car has hit the
guardrail and a telephone pole...

00:16:10.820 --> 00:16:14.090
...and the driver inside
is unconscious.

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:17.190
You can't be sure what injuries
have been sustained.

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:23.430
The door is locked. And the
engine's still running.

00:16:24.200 --> 00:16:25.930
How are you going to react
in this situation?

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:27.510
Sir!

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:30.300
I'll demonstrate!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.410
First...

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:36.540
I'll open the
door!

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:44.050
If the engine is running, and
I can't reach the key...

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:52.690
I'll call to the driver while trying to deter-
mine the extent of his injuries.

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:54.830
In this case, they're
minor injuries.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.470
Okay. What's
next?

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:02.540
A car made a sharp turn at an intersection,
and flipped onto its side.

00:17:09.850 --> 00:17:11.490
Lieutenant Toukairin.

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:12.090
Yes?

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:15.580
This training program is still too easy!

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:17.560
It is?

00:17:17.560 --> 00:17:20.930
Yes. And as such, it's meaningless.

00:17:31.410 --> 00:17:33.840
Now this is more like it!
A mega-pileup!

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:35.710
That's totally unrealistic!

00:17:36.710 --> 00:17:38.870
Let me explain.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:42.440
The car was speeding on a mountain
road, and miscalculated a corner.

00:17:42.550 --> 00:17:45.750
It lost control for a moment but eventually
came to a stop. However...!

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:49.910
The van behind it did not see the stopped
car, and ran right onto it.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:54.550
The car is hanging over the cliff, and
could fall over at any moment.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:57.430
Well, what do you think?

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.300
Not bad, not bad at all.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:17.480
Okay, stop! Ready?

00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:19.450
Ready!

00:18:22.720 --> 00:18:25.690
Are you all right?
He's conscious!

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:28.490
Yoriko, grab
that side.

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:30.630
Okay!

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:35.190
We've removed the victim!
Pull, Miyuki!

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:52.690
Stop, Miyuki!

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:08.500
I can't hold on
much longer!

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:17.040
Hurry!

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:19.740
I've got him!
He's out!

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:21.880
Let go!

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:29.890
Natsumi!

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.760
Are you all right, Officer
Tsujimoto?

00:19:41.940 --> 00:19:43.930
Natsumi! Are
you okay?

00:19:44.100 --> 00:19:46.070
Uh, yeah...

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:49.070
Oh.

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:52.110
Don't worry, it's merely a flesh wound.

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:53.480
We've got to take care of it!

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:55.310
Huh?

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.210
Uh... no, really!

00:19:57.380 --> 00:20:02.010
Wow, even you aren't invincible,
Lieutenant Toukairin.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:07.420
Emergency first aid really does
come in handy, doesn't it?

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.060
I'll just follow the same
steps as before.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:11.800
I'm really fine! Please!

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:12.300
You're not!

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:13.400
Please! Leave me alone!

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:13.830
Sit still!

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:15.100
Ow!

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:19.430
Stop! Not there! No!
Quit squirming around! Stay still!

00:20:22.680 --> 00:20:27.410
I'm just glad his injuries
weren't more serious.

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:29.180
I'm sorry, sir!

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:30.680
I'm very sorry, sir!

00:20:30.680 --> 00:20:31.410
Huh?

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:35.040
It's completely my fault, sir! It
was an unsafe environment.

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:37.520
I failed, as an officer,
and as an instructor.

00:20:37.690 --> 00:20:41.020
Just hang on a minute! I was
the one responsible...

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:44.100
...for making our training so unsafe, sir!

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:47.230
No, you rightly noted needless training!

00:20:47.400 --> 00:20:50.370
Yes, but I should've planned it better!

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:52.540
No, it was planned very well!

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:55.810
I winged it! Chief, I take full responsibility!

00:20:55.810 --> 00:20:57.710
You weren't responsible, Officer Tsujimoto!

00:20:57.710 --> 00:20:58.180
I was!

00:20:58.180 --> 00:20:58.750
Were not!

00:20:58.750 --> 00:20:59.250
Was!

00:20:59.250 --> 00:20:59.680
Were not!

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:00.250
Was!

00:21:00.250 --> 00:21:00.870
Were not!

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:04.210
It doesn't matter! Just be
more careful next time.

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:06.690
You can't say it doesn't matter!

00:21:06.690 --> 00:21:08.240
It's not right!

00:21:08.420 --> 00:21:10.290
Ugh...

00:21:10.460 --> 00:21:17.300
"An owner has been found."

00:21:21.640 --> 00:21:27.770
In the red corner, there's a large order of
porkchops on rice and liver with onions.

00:21:27.870 --> 00:21:32.810
In the blue corner, we've a large tempura
on rice, and a ramen entree.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:47.390
Oh well. Guess it can't hurt.

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.490
Ready?

00:21:49.600 --> 00:21:51.390
Go!

00:21:55.340 --> 00:22:01.470
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:11.380
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:18.330
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:28.400
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.470 --> 00:22:42.380
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:50.660
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:59.190
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.470 --> 00:23:07.260
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.370 --> 00:23:16.840
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:24.320
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:27.760
"Being on the ball!"

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:31.290
Hey, hey! Summer! That
means summer vacation!

00:23:31.830 --> 00:23:32.590
And the ocean!

00:23:32.770 --> 00:23:34.230
And... umm... the seashore!
"Beach Volleyball Death Match"

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:36.930
And th... the beach!

00:23:37.100 --> 00:23:38.500
Beach volleyball!

00:23:38.670 --> 00:23:40.300
Beach Volleyball Man!

00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:43.200
"Beach Volleyball Man?!"

00:23:43.380 --> 00:23:45.440
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 39...

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:46.450
..."Ah! The Springtime of Beach
Volleyball Man's Youth."

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:48.080
FILE. 39
AH! THE SPRINGTIME OF
BEACH VOLLEYBALL
MAN'S YOUTH

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:51.080
a... Nakajima is in it, too?!
